+# Extraction fidelity acceptance matrix
+
+Planning requirement updated from the completed audit. No files in this matrix were generated or processed during the documentation update. Native fixture execution still requires the explicit synthetic-only allowance in the amendment record.
+
+Assessed repository HEAD: 2dad59e0ee26ab6586f6a49ec1dfdb993d1f9ad7.
+
+## Supported scope
+
+Current upload admission permits PDF, DOCX, XLSX and TXT (src/lib/http.ts:78). Approved-source acquisition also supports its governed HTML/PDF route. Repository-owned content uses approved static/registry producers. This matrix does not add PPTX, arbitrary image uploads, legacy Office macros, encrypted-document decryption, executable spreadsheets, general web crawling or new source licences.
+
+DOCX needs native paragraph/table/media anchors; XLSX needs worksheet/cell/range anchors. Do not label those as physical PDF pages. Unsupported embedded features must have explicit limitations rather than silently promising extraction.
+
+Use synthetic, repository-owned or explicitly permitted fixtures. No patient information, live URLs, provider calls or external references should be resolved by the offline suite. Expected evidence must be authored independently of the extractor implementation.
+
+## Minimum representative matrix
+
+Six primary document/producer fixtures plus one lightweight text case can exercise the requested dimensions. Add variants to the same fixture rather than many near-duplicate files.
+
+| ID / class                                       | Important source content                                                                                                                                                                   | Admission and extraction expectation                                                                                                                                                                                             | Chunks / enrichment expectation                                                                                                                                                                                       | Persistence / eligibility / retrieval expectation                                                                                                                                                                                               |
+| ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| E1 Native PDF guideline                          | Two columns; headings; repeated running header; repeated legitimate recommendation; decimal 0.5; range; adult-only recommendation; child exclusion on next page; final appendix/reference. | All pages accounted for in original order; columns reconstructed correctly; running header distinguished from real repeated recommendation. Source units, reference target and final appendix retained.                          | Claim remains linked to population, strength, exception and units even across chunk/page boundaries. One/two/eight-item summary cases use actual producer adapter; original evidence remains available independently. | Stored canonical text/structure resolves exact anchors; all marked evidence atoms recoverable by evidence queries, including appendix; no generic overview accepted as substitute.                                                              |
+| E2 Mixed scanned/native PDF with visual evidence | A sparse scanned page; dense native page plus scanned insert; table with caption/units/footnote; simple flowchart; one native/OCR numeric disagreement; a low-quality late page.           | Expected pages and images inventoried. OCR attempts/engine/language/preprocessing recorded. Dense text does not hide the scanned insert. Native/OCR conflict preserved for conservative resolution.                              | Table cell/header/unit/footnote relation survives; image caption stays interpretation unless supported; flowchart branches not invented. Duplicate text does not become independent corroboration.                    | Low-confidence or unresolved material contradiction has a specific limitation and gate outcome. Pixel artifact and OCR/text anchors refer to same source version. Retrieval cannot cite an unverified image interpretation as established fact. |
+| E3 DOCX clinical reference                       | Heading hierarchy; table with merged header, unit and footnote; hyperlink source; image plus caption; repeated paragraph; late appendix.                                                   | Native paragraphs/tables and supported relationships retained; media mapped through document relationships; no fabricated physical page 1 lineage for everything. Unsupported layout features recorded.                          | Original table/paragraph boundaries survive; caption binds to image; late content remains reachable; repeated legitimate text retained where meaningful.                                                              | Anchor resolves paragraph/table/media in same version; semantic content survives serialisation. Explicit limited capability when a relationship cannot be reconstructed.                                                                        |
+| E4 XLSX clinical table                           | Two sheets; sparse cells; merged heading; numeric 0.5; percent/unit format; formula with cached result; formula without cached result; rich text/hyperlink; final row restriction.         | Formula/value/format are separate; no formula execution or external fetch. Cached result used only with provenance; absent result is not fabricated. Rich text and hyperlink display text survive. Cell/range identity retained. | Row/header/unit/footnote relationship remains expressible; no [object Object] evidence. Empty-cell position does not shift values under a different header. Last row not lost.                                        | Worksheet and cell/range anchors resolve; unsupported or missing formula results are explicit. Evidence query returns the correct value with unit, sheet and qualification.                                                                     |
+| E5 Approved HTML source snapshot                 | Main article, qualifying aside, table, caption/footnote, source hyperlink, navigation/footer and embedded instruction-like content.                                                        | Existing policy/acquisition adapter consumes saved bytes offline; preserves relevant structure and references; scripts/navigation excluded; no source contacted. Retained artifact conforms to its licence/retention policy.     | Table/qualifier survives transformation; links remain source references; untrusted instructions stay data. Source and generated plain/structured representation retain one lineage.                                   | Exact source/representation/policy hashes and transform version stored. Retrieval resolves retained evidence; original/derivative counted once. Disallowed host/version/content stays blocked even if syntactically valid.                      |
+| E6 Repository static + registry derivative       | One canonical eligible static record; one registry derivative from E1 with content >8,000 characters and a late restriction; a deliberately ineligible draft record.                       | Actual source producer builds complete evidence content, separately from any preview. Seed and dynamic publication paths are exercised; original source identity carried through.                                                | Late restriction retained; release/epoch identity attached to correct body; no independent corroboration from derivative. Ineligible record stays ineligible.                                                         | Same permitted release resolves body and lineage; candidate/withdrawn/draft excluded. Original + derivative form one evidence family; a separate independent source remains separate.                                                           |
+| E7 TXT control                                   | UTF-8 text with ligature/Unicode, repeated whitespace, dehyphenation edge, standalone threshold and late section.                                                                          | Full text within budget preserved with raw/canonical mapping; TXT is not assumed to have physical pages.                                                                                                                         | Numeric/punctuation distinctions survive normalisation/deduplication; no unsupported enrichment.                                                                                                                      | Persisted coordinates recover exact intended excerpt; optional structural limitations visible; correct tail evidence is retrievable.                                                                                                            |
+
+These are small authored fixtures; no representative population-performance claim follows from passing them. Select later real-document examples by observed intake mix and known failure risk under separate authority.
+
+## Shared RAG reference acceptance
+
+The adopted [R1–R5/H1–H7 handoff](rag-evidence-handoff.md) reuses E1–E7. Add supported explanation versus invented causal relation, primary-complete/partial/restricted/supplements-disabled cases, reviewed-conflict versus unknown status, and supplement removal preserving independently supported material. Follow actual producer output through supplier stages; RAG owns packed evidence, every displayed claim, elaboration and complete display/copy. Use content-free counts/versions/typed reasons to distinguish extraction, packing, generation, verification and display loss. A supplier pass is not model usefulness or ordinary Answer acceptance.
+
+## Stage assertions shared across every route
+
+| Stage                     | Evidence to record                                                                                                                       | Minimum discriminating assertion                                                                                                                                            |
+| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Admission                 | Content identity, route, actor/service, owner/staging scope, source authority/rights/currentness, policy and supported feature decision. | Retry creates one durable event; stale/denied authority does not become cleared. Unsupported features are rejected or explicitly limited.                                   |
+| Expected source inventory | Page/sheet/section count and nominated tables/images/claims/references, including final unit.                                            | Every expected unit is retained, deliberately excluded, failed or skipped with a reason. A count without identity is insufficient.                                          |
+| Extraction/OCR            | Raw and canonical evidence, method/version, unit IDs, confidence where available, native/OCR alternatives, limits.                       | Marked source evidence appears without material distortion; unresolved disagreement remains unresolved.                                                                     |
+| Structural reconstruction | Reading order, table coordinates, headings, caption/footnote links, source references, normalisation mapping.                            | Intended relationships survive, including negative controls that would be wrong if row/column/qualifier were detached.                                                      |
+| Chunks/index units        | Stable evidence identity, boundaries, contextual links and exact source anchors.                                                         | Each marked claim has access to its required qualification; text remains original evidence, not just summary.                                                               |
+| Summary/labels            | Actual provider-shaped response through the real adapter, projection, nested validation and explicit support status.                     | Valid detailed producer output passes. Shape-valid unsupported numerical/population reversal cannot be presented as semantically verified.                                  |
+| Persistence               | Complete immutable generation/release, artifact hashes and exact source/policy/owner association.                                        | Serialisation/round trip resolves all retained evidence; stale completion cannot overwrite a newer generation or erase the prior valid set.                                 |
+| Eligibility/activation    | Technical gate result with exact version, limitations and lifecycle authority.                                                           | Incomplete/unsafe/revoked evidence cannot pass as complete/active. Technical eligibility does not silently create clinical approval.                                        |
+| Retrieval                 | Real producer candidate plus evidence resolution in one snapshot, role, lineage and limitations.                                         | Return the marked evidence for each probe; exclude withdrawn/private/staging/unsupported candidates before ranking; do not substitute another source silently.              |
+| Ordinary Answer           | Separate RAG integration fixture and later authorised model/user evaluation.                                                             | Detailed answer uses the right evidence and qualifications; reports limits and distinguishes primary/derivative/supplementary roles. Not part of a default-off kernel pass. |
+
+## Boundary and recovery variants
+
+Apply only to relevant fixtures, keeping the matrix small.
+
+| Variant                                                           | Expected outcome                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |
+| ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| Content just below / at / above a configured cap                  | Explicit whole-operation resource failure or precise partial limitation with gate exclusion. No unmarked first-N complete result. Verify table-text, row, column metadata and recovered-row caps independently.                      |
+| Error only in a late page/row/appendix                            | Error visible even when overall text density is high. No summary sampling or average score masks it.                                                                                                                                 |
+| Qualification just outside a chunk, sample or context prefix      | Qualification remains linked, or output is withheld/limited. After-900-character model-visible cache changes must invalidate reuse.                                                                                                  |
+| Same image, changed nearby meaning                                | Complete effective request identity changes; prior caption is not reused as equivalent.                                                                                                                                              |
+| Identical bytes under changed rights/policy/currentness           | No access/egress reuse bypass. Reprocessing plan differentiates content recomputation from eligibility invalidation.                                                                                                                 |
+| Native/OCR decimal, sign or population conflict                   | Both provenance tracks preserved; no concatenation-based corroboration; gate or explicit uncertainty reflects conflict.                                                                                                              |
+| Duplicate retry, expired lease, reclaimed job with same worker ID | One current attempt owns mutations; stale attempt rejected without touching sibling work.                                                                                                                                            |
+| Provider success followed by persistence failure                  | Safe bounded retry/finalisation; no repeated extraction unless upstream evidence is invalid.                                                                                                                                         |
+| G1 summary returns after G2 activation                            | G1 cannot overwrite G2 summary/labels/metadata; prior valid generation remains consistent.                                                                                                                                           |
+| Cancellation during extraction/caption/embedding                  | Bounded cancellation/lease checking; no late completion; task-owned temporary artifacts have governed cleanup.                                                                                                                       |
+| Cleanup races activation or rollback                              | Active/retained/newly referenced resources remain protected; withdrawn content cannot be restored by rollback.                                                                                                                       |
+| Queue exceeds document/task/page limits                           | Stable cursor walks all authorised tasks exactly once; counts and “empty” status are truthful.                                                                                                                                       |
+| Valid difficult input versus hostile input                        | Supported complex DOCX/XLSX/PDF passes within limits; malformed package, macro/external-content relationship and resource abuse fail with actionable reasons. No scanners or remote URLs required for these existing fixture checks. |
+
+## Acceptance metrics
+
+For this finite matrix, require:
+
+1. **100% of nominated critical evidence atoms and relationships preserved on positive supported fixtures; negative/incomplete variants withheld with their expected reason.** Report preserved, withheld and missing counts separately against independently authored source expectations. Withholding a supported positive fixture cannot pass. “Withheld” does not count as successful extraction or eligibility.
+2. **Zero unsupported critical relationships marked supported**, including dose, unit, polarity, population, recommendation strength and table alignment mutations.
+3. **Every exposed anchor resolves** against the correct persisted version and coordinate system. Unresolvable or approximate anchors are marked as such and cannot masquerade as exact.
+4. **Zero silent limit losses.** Expected counts, actual counts and reasons reconcile.
+5. **Zero stale writes or scope violations** in the selected executable concurrency/permission schedules once those tests are authorised.
+6. **Zero false corroboration** from original/derivative pairs in the selected lineage cases.
+7. **No automatic inheritance of the U02 offline exception.** New failures are classified at the changed unit's exact code/dependency boundary.
+
+Do not collapse these into one weighted quality percentage that allows a severe missing contraindication to be offset by many correct paragraphs. Keep failures and coverage denominators visible.
+
+## Smallest credible execution tiers
+
+- During implementation: one failing producer/adapter regression, then the affected focused selector.
+- Extraction proof: existing local extractors using synthetic fixture bytes and permitted temporary outputs, only after implementation/testing authority.
+- Persistence/permissions/concurrency: separately authorised disposable local database with actual SQL and controlled interleavings. Mock RPC argument tests are necessary but insufficient.
+- Provider parity: separately authorised, bounded comparison after local evidence is sound; count calls/cost and preserve failed cases.
+- Hosted/clinical/Answer: separately authorised exact-deployment and source-governance acceptance. Never infer these from local fixture success.
+
+Nothing in this planning document authorises executing a tier. The documentation update is complete separately from future product, native extraction, local SQL and connected acceptance.
