+# Ingestion smart-agent allocation for future authorised execution
+
+Allocation adopted under [current execution authority](2026-09-07-execution-authority.md). Serial local dispatch and commits are authorised after independent plan review and capability preflight. Record observed route evidence in execution artifacts; do not infer it from this table. Models below are planned routes, not observed executions. Implementation stays at least High; any stronger task/phase floor wins. Concrete amendment and final whole-range formal review stay xhigh.
+
+| Work/unit                                                | Proposed writer                                                                                   | Required review roles retained from continuation; sensitive additions                                                                                                                |
+| -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| Controller                                               | Astra High                                                                                        | Accountable integration/authority decisions; independent review still required                                                                                                       |
+| U01                                                      | None — retain accepted work                                                                       | Historical ingestion-worker + schema guardian retained, not rerun                                                                                                                    |
+| U02 corrective packet                                    | Astra High                                                                                        | ingestion-worker-reviewer + clinical-governance-reviewer                                                                                                                             |
+| U03 fencing                                              | Astra High                                                                                        | ingestion-worker-reviewer + supabase-schema-guardian + clinical-governance-reviewer                                                                                                  |
+| U04 staging/evaluation                                   | Astra High                                                                                        | ingestion-worker-reviewer + supabase-schema-guardian + rag-retrieval-reviewer                                                                                                        |
+| U05 lifecycle                                            | Astra High                                                                                        | supabase-schema-guardian + ingestion-worker-reviewer                                                                                                                                 |
+| U06 runbooks                                             | Sol High, only settled behaviour                                                                  | clinical-governance-reviewer; technical owner consulted where lifecycle wording changes                                                                                              |
+| U07 admission                                            | Astra High                                                                                        | supabase-schema-guardian + clinical-governance-reviewer                                                                                                                              |
+| U08 safety/egress                                        | Astra High                                                                                        | ingestion-worker-reviewer + clinical-governance-reviewer                                                                                                                             |
+| U09 fidelity                                             | Astra High                                                                                        | ingestion-worker-reviewer retained; clinical-governance-reviewer for F03 support/critical expectations and rag-retrieval-reviewer for changed source-span/lineage consumer contracts |
+| U10 eligibility                                          | Astra High                                                                                        | supabase-schema-guardian + ingestion-worker-reviewer + clinical-governance-reviewer                                                                                                  |
+| U11 queue/UI                                             | Sol High for settled presentation/pagination; Astra High for permission/mutation/repair ambiguity | frontend-ui-reviewer + supabase-schema-guardian retained; ingestion-worker-reviewer for repair/fencing changes                                                                       |
+| U12 resolver/kernel                                      | Astra High                                                                                        | rag-retrieval-reviewer + supabase-schema-guardian + clinical-governance-reviewer                                                                                                     |
+| U13 recovery/invalidation                                | Astra High                                                                                        | ingestion-worker-reviewer + supabase-schema-guardian; rag-retrieval-reviewer for cache/withdrawal consumer changes                                                                   |
+| Mechanical source/hash/fixture specification preparation | Terra Medium read-only, when briefing overhead is justified                                       | Controller verifies result; not implementation, clinical judgment or formal acceptance                                                                                               |
+| Canonical documentation amendment formal review          | Independent Astra xhigh                                                                           | Clinical governance plus relevant schema/ingestion/retrieval authority expertise; no implementation agents now                                                                       |
+| Core tranche                                             | Fresh reviewers at required floors, Astra for sensitive review                                    | ingestion-worker-reviewer, supabase-schema-guardian, rag-retrieval-reviewer                                                                                                          |
+| Trusted tranche                                          | Fresh reviewers at required floors                                                                | clinical-governance-reviewer, supabase-schema-guardian, ingestion-worker-reviewer, rag-retrieval-reviewer, frontend-ui-reviewer                                                      |
+| C06 whole-range                                          | Fresh Astra xhigh specialists                                                                     | clinical-governance-reviewer, supabase-schema-guardian, rag-retrieval-reviewer, ingestion-worker-reviewer; verification-router for gate selection                                    |
+
+Routine independent review may use Sol High where the actual diff and formal floor allow it. Sensitive schema/privacy/clinical/concurrency/retrieval review uses Astra High or xhigh as required. Reviewer role and model are separate dimensions; selecting a cheaper role name does not change intrinsic risk. No unknown unit receives a default permissive route. Higher-effort architecture/SQL/lease decisions retain their applicable floor even inside a High implementation task.
+
+Use controller + at most two children by default. While one writer works, one read-only scout may prepare the next unit from frozen accepted source/hash inputs. After the writer freezes the complete range, two reviewers may inspect independent specialties, followed by later waves until every mandatory specialty is covered. A third child slot requires a concrete independent use and controller release; do not treat available capacity as reserved capacity. No recursive spawning, no overlapping writers, no review of moving files and no bypass of coordinator leases.
+
+One designated gate owner runs each check; all reviewers use the same command/result/head/dependency package. They may request a missing discriminating check but do not each repeat the same suite. All final task/tranche/continuation reviews still judge the complete corrected original range; unchanged evidence reuse cannot turn this into correction-only review.
+
+New units use fresh implementers. Correction rounds 1–3 use the same suitable writer with exact findings, current diff and failure history. Diagnose missing context, broken commands, dependencies and contention before attributing failure to model capability. Repair context first; repeated substantive failures in rounds 4–5 justify controlled fresh escalation. At round 6 stop automatic redispatch and have the controller resolve cause/scope/decision; it does not waive unresolved Critical/Important findings. Stale/unavailable writer context is an explicit reason for replacement, not automatic churn.
+
+Every future brief records unit, immutable original base, current allowed paths, boundaries, frozen source inputs, risk/floor, planned route, exact checks and stop conditions. Every report records returned agent identity and actual route only when exposed by execution telemetry. A tool accepting a requested route is not proof it ran; unavailable model/effort evidence stays unavailable and blocks a formal route claim. No invented tool parameters, recursive agents, provider access or implicit task messages.
+
+Compatibility is deliberately limited. The parent P-phase checker does not currently establish U/C phase acceptance or this new allocation. Use a reviewed manual continuation record and the existing canonical full-range review-package writer, preserving old hashes. Do not mutate `programme-manifest.json`, inject unknown receipt fields, invoke `--accept-phase C01`/`--resume U03`, lower floors or copy the other RAG worktree's helper. Any requested automation extension needs a separate small implementation/verification task. The execution environment and evidence compatibility must be checked before any authorised first use.
